cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this work using the version metadata in this file."
title: "Progress on Turyn's converse: general symmetry theorems and coverage below 10,000"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Kline
    given-names: Jeffery
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/turyn-converse-progress"
url: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/turyn-converse-progress"
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  General symmetry theorems for symmetric Turyn pairs, including an index-two
  prime-fibre obstruction and an obstruction to inverting a C_3 factor on every
  odd abelian cofactor, combined with multiplier theorems, exact quotient tests
  and certificates. The collected arguments exclude 655 of the 663
  non-prime-power parameters q < 10000 with q = 1 mod 4 that are sums of two
  squares; eight remain open, the smallest 3965. The converse remains open.
keywords:
  - Turyn pairs
  - negacyclic conference matrices
  - relative difference sets
  - multiplier theorem
  - Hadamard matrices
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Toward a converse of Turyn's theorem: obstructions to Turyn pairs at composite orders"
    authors:
      - family-names: Kline
        given-names: Jeffery
    version: 0.2.0
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21776269
